{"uid":"3edff2865447cec6","name":"test_three_consecutive_commit_only_iterations_never_force_verify_dispatch","fullName":"tests.test_worker_hat#test_three_consecutive_commit_only_iterations_never_force_verify_dispatch","historyId":"12b25ae8a6ed3fc01bc784f4e86f6817","time":{"start":1791976558533,"stop":1791976559339,"duration":806},"description":"Task 004 (v0.20.1 PRD requirement B.2, gate finding VG-002): the\n    replacement for the three retired v0.19 B.2 hand-off nodes this module\n    used to pin --\n    `test_three_consecutive_commit_only_iterations_hand_the_task_to_verify`,\n    `test_a_lower_configured_threshold_fires_sooner` and\n    `test_a_broken_streak_resets_the_counter_and_needs_a_fresh_run` (see\n    `docs/test-suite-audit.md` \"Subsumed\" for the mapping).\n    A vigilant task carrying `estimatedIterations: 3` runs exactly three\n    consecutive worker iterations, each landing a real commit and\n    reporting the worker contract's `{\"verdict\": \"no_verdict\"}` (\"still\n    working\") and nothing else, never a completion signal -- the exact\n    shape that used to force\n    `awaiting-validation` and dispatch `verify` on the worker's own behalf\n    the instant the third one landed (`LoopSupervisor._record_task_\n    absorption_streak`, deleted in this same commit). Now nothing does:\n    the task is still `in-progress` after all three of them, `verify`\n    never ran at all, and the `notes` field never grows the legacy\n    hand-off sentence. `estimatedIterations: 3` also puts the task's own\n    progress budget (`estimatedIterations + 2` = 5) safely ABOVE the three\n    iterations driven here, so what this node observes is the absence of\n    the deleted streak and nothing else -- no forced split is in play.\n    Governing\n    what SHOULD happen once a task genuinely exhausts its budget is the\n    pre-existing progress-budget/forced-split path (task 016) -- pinned\n    for THIS shape by tasks 005/006 (requirements B.3/B.4), never this\n    test's own job.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 004 (v0.20.1 PRD requirement B.2, gate finding VG-002): the<br />\nreplacement for the three retired v0.19 B.2 hand-off nodes this module<br />\nused to pin --<br />\n<code>test_three_consecutive_commit_only_iterations_hand_the_task_to_verify</code>,<br />\n<code>test_a_lower_configured_threshold_fires_sooner</code> and<br />\n<code>test_a_broken_streak_resets_the_counter_and_needs_a_fresh_run</code> (see<br />\n<code>docs/test-suite-audit.md</code> &quot;Subsumed&quot; for the mapping).<br />\nA vigilant task carrying <code>estimatedIterations: 3</code> runs exactly three<br />\nconsecutive worker iterations, each landing a real commit and<br />\nreporting the worker contract's <code>{&quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;no_verdict&quot;}</code> (&quot;still<br />\nworking&quot;) and nothing else, never a completion signal -- the exact<br />\nshape that used to force<br />\n<code>awaiting-validation</code> and dispatch <code>verify</code> on the worker's own behalf<br />\nthe instant the third one landed (<code>LoopSupervisor._record_task_ absorption_streak</code>, deleted in this same commit). Now nothing does:<br />\nthe task is still <code>in-progress</code> after all three of them, <code>verify</code><br />\nnever ran at all, and the <code>notes</code> field never grows the legacy<br />\nhand-off sentence. <code>estimatedIterations: 3</code> also puts the task's own<br />\nprogress budget (<code>estimatedIterations + 2</code> = 5) safely ABOVE the three<br />\niterations driven here, so what this node observes is the absence of<br />\nthe deleted streak and nothing else -- no forced split is in play.<br />\nGoverning<br />\nwhat SHOULD happen once a task genuinely exhausts its budget is the<br />\npre-existing progress-budget/forced-split path (task 016) -- pinned<br />\nfor THIS shape by tasks 005/006 (requirements B.3/B.4), never this<br />\ntest's own job.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,